  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1222 AM MST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nUpper ridge building across the Rockies will bring warmer and\ndrier weather to the region Wed, then a weak upper trough and\ncold front drops temps back slightly on Thanksgiving day, though\nconditions will remain dry. Ridge flattens and upper jet sags \nback southward toward CO over the weekend, though models differ \non the timing of how quickly this happens. In any event, main \nfeature of this pattern will be warm and increasingly breezy \nconditions from Friday onward, with potentially a few bouts of \nsnow showers along the Continental Divide, mainly from Monarch \nPass northward.",
